👑 Root User – Description

Root User is the original owner of an AWS account.

It is created when you first sign up for AWS using your email address.
The Root User has complete and unrestricted access to all AWS services and resources.

It can manage:
Billing and payments
AWS services
Security settings
IAM users and permissions
The Root User should not be used for daily work.
For security, create an IAM User for regular AWS activities.
Simple Definition

Root User is the main AWS account owner with full access and control over all AWS services and resources.

The Root User has complete control over the AWS account, so 
its key security precautions are enabling MFA, protecting the credentials, and avoiding daily use are essential.
